---
import Base from "@/layouts/Base.astro";
import { DRAFT_DAYS, RETENTION_MONTHS } from "@/lib/retention";

// California's online privacy law (Business and Professions Code §22575)
// requires a site that collects personal information from California
// consumers to post this, whatever the size of the business. Every
// statement here describes what the site and its server actually do; a
// change to either is a change to this page. Both periods below are the
// numbers the code enforces, read from src/lib/retention.ts: submissions
// by src/lib/db.ts, drafts by src/lib/forms/enhance.ts.
const effective = "2026-10-05";
const effectiveLabel = "October 5, 2026";
---

<Base title="Privacy" description="What this site collects when you send a form, what it is used for, who else handles it, and how long it is kept." mainClass="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 pt-32 pb-24">
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-navy sm:text-4xl">Privacy</h1>
  <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-muted">Effective <time datetime={effective}>{effectiveLabel}</time></p>

  <div class="mt-10 space-y-10 text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted">
    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-navy">What this site collects</h2>
      <p class="mt-3">
        Only what you send in a form. The quote form asks for your name, a phone number or email, the services you're interested in, and anything you want to tell me. The phone-bill audit form asks for your business name, your name, a phone number or email, your monthly bill range, and anything else you add.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3">
        Nothing else is collected. There are no cookies, no analytics, no ads and no tracking scripts, and every font and image is served from this site rather than a third party.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3">
        While you fill in a form, what you type is saved in your own browser so a reload or a closed tab doesn't lose it. It stays on your device and is cleared once you send the form. If it sits untouched for {DRAFT_DAYS} days, it is discarded the next time you open that form instead of being filled back in.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3">
        Like any web server, this one keeps a log of requests: the address they came from, the browser, the page and the time. The log is kept for 14 days, to keep the site secure and working.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-navy">How it's used</h2>
      <p class="mt-3">
        To reply to you about what you asked, and for nothing else. It is never sold or rented, never shared for marketing, and never added to a mailing list.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-navy">Who else handles it</h2>
      <p class="mt-3">
        What you send is stored on Vigario Technology Solutions' own server. A notification with the same details is emailed to me so I can reply, so it also passes through the email providers that deliver, forward and hold my mail. No one else receives it.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-navy">How long it's kept</h2>
      <p class="mt-3">
        Submissions are deleted automatically after {RETENTION_MONTHS} months, and backups of the database roll off on their own schedule after that. A copy of each notification stays in my email until I delete it.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-navy">Seeing, correcting or deleting what you sent</h2>
      <p class="mt-3">
        Email <a href="mailto:admin@vigario.tech" class="text-accent-ink underline hover:text-navy">admin@vigario.tech</a> and I'll tell you what I have, correct it, or delete it, whichever you ask for.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-navy">Do Not Track</h2>
      <p class="mt-3">
        This site doesn't track visitors across other sites or over time, so there is nothing for a Do Not Track signal to turn off. Every visitor is treated the same way, whether or not their browser sends one.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-navy">Changes</h2>
      <p class="mt-3">
        If this policy changes, the effective date at the top changes with it, and anything that changes what is collected or how it's used will be described here.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
